<div class="container">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="about-image">
    <img src="/public/headshot.jpg" alt="Dominic Critchlow" />
  </div>

  <div class="about-content">

    <p>I build AI products and get them into people's hands. For most of my career that meant the Department of Defense; these days it's private-sector clients.</p>

    <p>Right now I'm a forward-deployed product manager at <a href="https://fractional.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fractional AI</a> in New York, leading engagements that put custom LLM products into production for private-equity clients. On the side, I teach a graduate Big Data Analytics course at Seton Hall's Stillman School of Business and serve as a Military Intelligence officer in the U.S. Army Reserve.</p>

    <p>Before this, I spent nearly a decade in the defense world. At Booz Allen I led a 60-person engineering organization out of Stuttgart, Germany, delivering AI-enabled decision systems across U.S. European and Africa Commands. Before that, at the DoD's Chief Digital and AI Office, I co-founded <a href="https://github.com/dod-advana/gamechanger" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gamechanger</a>, an AI-powered policy search platform. I built the MVP solo, grew it to 1,500 users and a 25-person team, and it was recognized by the National Security Commission on AI. Along the way I shipped software for NASA. I spend a lot of time thinking about how human and computer interaction is evolving.</p>

    <p>I got my start studying physics and computer science at Austin Peay State University in Tennessee, where I launched weather balloons and wrote Python scripts to chase them across the sky.</p>

    <p>Outside of work I like to experiment: <a href="/pinned/">iOS apps</a>, <a href="/helio/">data visualizations</a>, and <a href="/airwave-ml/">radio + machine learning projects</a> that start as a simple question and turn into something useful, or at least fun. I think good technology should solve real problems and leave people a little more curious along the way.</p>

    <p>The best way to reach me is <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dominic-critchlow/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>. You can also find me on <a href="https://github.com/DomCritchlow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
  </div>
